      <section id="sect-00002">
        <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
        <section class="practice" id="sect-00005"><title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
<exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00009">
          <problem id="prob-00013">
            <para id="para-00054">What quadratic equation of the form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> would have the solutions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00013">
            <para id="para-00055">Enter the quadratic equation.</para>
            <para id="para-00056">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00057"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>23</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Working backward, these are solutions to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. In standard form, this is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>23</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <note class="self-check" id="note-00002">
        <exercise id="exer-00011">
          <problem id="prob-00015">
          <para id="para-00058"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_9_5_3_SC"/></para>
          </problem>
          </exercise>
         
      </note>
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Additional Resources</title>
        <section id="sect-00004">
          <title>Using the Calculator for Approximate Solutions</title>
          <para id="para-00059">Let's look at the solutions to the equations from 9.5.2: Additional Resources:</para>
          <para id="para-00060">A more compact way to write the two solutions to the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00061">How large or small are those numbers? Are they positive or negative? We can use a calculator to compute the approximate values of both expressions:</para>
          <para id="para-00062"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.683</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7.317</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00063">We can also approximate the solutions by graphing. The equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, so we can graph the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and find its zeros by locating the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph.</para>
          <para id="para-00064">
                  <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_07_08_01.svg"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <note class="try" id="note-00003">
            <title>Try It: Using the Calculator for Approximate Solutions</title>
        <exercise id="exer-00010">
              <problem id="prob-00014">
                <para id="para-00065">Approximate the solutions to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>19</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
                <para id="para-00066">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
              </problem>
              <solution id="sol-00014">
                <para id="para-00067">Here is how to approximate the solutions:</para>
                <para id="para-00068"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Write two expressions. </para><para id="para-00070"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>19</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>19</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                <para id="para-00069"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Use the calculator to approximate the solutions to three decimal places. </para><para id="para-00071"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.359</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mn>7.359</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              </solution>
            </exercise>
          </note>
        </section>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>